today marks two weeks since the death of  george floyd  massive nationwide protest are showing  no signs of slowing down and now there  are calls all around the country  to defund police departments amid  demonstrations in minneapolis where  floyd was killed  a majority of city council members  announced plans to dismantle the  department there  in favor of a new system of public  safety they did not say though what that  may look like  the city's mayor does not support the  idea and he was booed during a weekend  rally  in washington today democratic lawmakers  are expected to introduce legislation  that would overhaul  police departments across the country  among the changes it would ban the use  of chokeholds  to subdue suspects and make it easier to  prosecute officers  for police brutality  attorney general william barr told face  to nation yesterday that he believes  systemic racism is not a problem in u.s  law enforcement  congresswoman val demings who used to be  orlando's police chief calls it the  ghost in the room  the florida democrat is on the short  list of potential running mates for  presumptive presidential nominee joe  biden and congresswoman demings joins us  now  from orlando congresswoman good morning  a lot of news to get to i want to start  with the news out of minneapolis uh  the city council voting to dismantle not  just  defund but dismantle and rebuild the  police department there  is that a strategy you could agree with  well first of all let me say good  morning to you and everyone it's good to  be  uh with you there are a lot of things  being proposed throughout the nation and  i think it's the direct result of people  being  hurt disappointed at what happened to mr  floyd  that's all too familiar to them but also  angry and demanding change and i do  believe that  everyone has a right to look at any  proposal  that is put forth because there  desperately needs to  be changed i i also believe that the  council is being very thoughtful  in terms of looking at all of the  services that police provide  you know there are some cases that  statutorily law enforcement is  responsible for  investigating they do a lot of things  associated with natural disasters and  terrorism  and so what i believe the council along  with  law enforcement authorities and other  community leaders will sit down  and look at everything and come out with  the plan that allows them to keep  minneapolis safe but also  bring the community and the police  together in a much needed and long  overdue way  yeah so congresswoman you mentioned the  context there and you also mentioned  that there are statutes that call police  into situations where a badge and a gun  may not be necessary  so on the on the question of defunding  the police what many people mean is move  that money  out of law enforcement hands and into  another sort of community engagement  fund  do you support that strategy  you know as i've listened to what has  occurred and watched what has occurred  certainly  over the last two weeks what happened to  mr floyd  there is no one on planet earth i hope  that believes anything about that  situation should have happened a lot  went wrong there but i'm also reminded  of the words of former chief david brown  out of dallas texas  when he had five of his officers  executed and he said something to this  effect that  every time society fails the police are  called in to  fix it and we all know usually by the  time the police are called  something has already gone drastically  wrong  within society and look as a former law  enforcement officer and as a police  chief  i know that the police are pulled to  respond to  situations on the street and in  communities that they are not prepared  to respond to  and not trained quite frankly to respond  to while they have received  several amounts of training and critical  incident debriefing dealing with mental  health  persons who are suffering from mental  health issues i do believe there is  opportunity here for the police and the  community to  come together and kind of spread look at  the responsibilities things that police  are taking on  that they were never supposed to take on  in the first place  and come out with a better plan  congresswoman  yeah it sounds like you're not using the  words defund the police but in terms of  narrowing the scope of the police  mission it sounds like you do agree that  that could be  in the future of this country i want to  talk about the bigger future of this  country and the past attorney general  barr  says systemic racism is not present in  law enforcement other administrative  administration officials have said the  same thing how can you fix a problem  that  roughly half the leadership does not  recognize exists  well you know i've said it multiple  times  long before the tragedy that happened  with mr floyd that racism  is and continues to be the ghost in the  room and look  i hear what uh attorney general barr is  saying  i don't believe he believes that i  believe that is just a talking point and  unfortunately  when you fail to publicly admit that  there is a problem  then it is extremely difficult to  address the problem and i've also said  that the president and certainly the top  cop i.e  william barr have a direct  responsibility to intervene  and say that yes we have a problem but  we're going to put the full weight  of the white house and the department of  justice to  fixing it to ride in it and to showing  compassion  and bringing the country together  unfortunately i don't believe the  president nor the attorney general have  the capability of doing that and  certainly  if they are continuing to stand at the  microphone on a public and international  stage  and say there is no problem then quite  frankly i think that they have served  their usefulness  for this country congresswoman demings  we we do have to go but i can't let you  go without asking you have you spoken  to former vice president joe biden  lately and what has he said  well i'm not going to share any personal  conversations that i have or had not  i have not had with the vice president  but look i am absolutely honored to be  considered  to run along uh side joe biden and i'll  leave it there  okay all right neither confirming or  denying the conversations are underway  congresswoman val demings very well done  uh  thank you very much we'll have to leave  it there
 

